1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,460
Kaeden: Hello Charlotte. I'm Kaeden, one of the supervisors. Welcome to the team.

2
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:07,010
Charlotte: Hi Aiden.

3
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:08,190
Kaeden: It's Kaeden.

4
00:00:08,190 --> 00:00:09,870
Charlotte: I'm so sorry.

5
00:00:09,870 --> 00:00:12,200
Kaeden: Don't worry. People often get my name wrong

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,949
they never know how to spell it.

7
00:00:16,949 --> 00:00:21,530
It's K-A-E-D-E-N, in case you ever need to write it.

8
00:00:21,530 --> 00:00:23,700
Charlotte: I'll try and remember.

9
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:28,033
Kaeden: So, there are a few practical things you need to sort out this morning.

10
00:00:28,033 --> 00:00:31,500
Then I'll show you what you're going to do today.

11
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:35,617
Charlotte: The email I received said to go to the front desk,

12
00:00:35,617 --> 00:00:39,390
to show my letter of appointment and pick up my badge.

13
00:00:39,390 --> 00:00:45,050
Kaeden: You'll need that for the staffroom and other areas of the supermarket where shoppers aren't allowed.

14
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:50,490
Kaeden: So, after you've finished at the front desk, I'll take you to the staffroom.

15
00:00:50,490 --> 00:00:55,610
Put your coat and rucksack in one of the lockers there. Take whichever one is free.

16
00:00:55,610 --> 00:00:57,620
Charlotte: Will I have a key?

17
00:00:57,620 --> 00:01:01,240
Kaeden: Yes. Try not to lose it. At the end of the day

18
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:04,080
leave it in the door for the next person to use.

19
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:05,370
Charlotte: Will do.

20
00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:10,510
Kaeden: You also need to go to the HR department to see Tiffany. She's really helpful.

21
00:01:10,510 --> 00:01:13,680
Charlotte: I was told to bring my passport with me

22
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:17,110
HR need to take a note of the number in it.

23
00:01:17,110 --> 00:01:19,860
Kaeden: That's right. Or you can show your ID card.

24
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:21,620
Charlotte: I don't have one of those.

25
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:24,355
Kaeden: OK. Tiffany will give you a uniform.

26
00:01:24,355 --> 00:01:29,140
They have lots in different sizes, so you just tell her what you need.

27
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:32,920
Kaeden: I won't come with you to HR - I've got to go and sort something else out

28
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:35,610
Problem with a bread slicer.

29
00:01:35,610 --> 00:01:38,980
Charlotte: Is the HR office near the staffroom?

30
00:01:38,980 --> 00:01:40,680
Kaeden: The staffroom's on the first floor

31
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:45,168
and HR are a couple of floors above that, on the third floor.

32
00:01:45,168 --> 00:01:47,230
There's a staircase outside the staffroom.

33
00:01:47,230 --> 00:01:48,510
Charlotte: OK.

34
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:49,760
Kaeden: When you've finished with HR

35
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:52,990
come and find me in the bakery section of the shop.

36
00:01:52,990 --> 00:01:55,520
Charlotte: I'm looking forward to getting started.

37
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:59,120
Kaeden: I'll just give you my phone number, in case you can't find me

38
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:01,240
Have you got your phone there?

39
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:05,090
Charlotte: Yes... OK, ready.

40
00:02:05,090 --> 00:02:12,550
Kaeden: It's oh-four-one-two double-six-five nine-oh-three.

41
00:02:12,550 --> 00:02:14,890
Charlotte: OK, done.

42
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:19,590
Kaeden: So, Charlotte, your tasks today are in the bakery section,

43
00:02:19,590 --> 00:02:24,290
on the sushi counter, and on the meat and fish counters.

44
00:02:24,290 --> 00:02:28,303
Kaeden: The first job is to check sell-by dates on the bread and cakes.

45
00:02:28,303 --> 00:02:32,890
If any of the dates are today's, put a new price label on the packaging.

46
00:02:32,890 --> 00:02:37,380
Charlotte: What if any of the labels are yesterday's dates, or older

47
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:40,180
Do I throw those items away?

48
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:43,946
Kaeden: Yes, but that shouldn't happen - we check the stock every day.

49
00:02:43,946 --> 00:02:45,800
When something needs a new price label

50
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:49,450
put a yellow one on the package, next to the original price.

51
00:02:49,450 --> 00:02:50,600
Charlotte: OK.

52
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:54,490
Kaeden: After that, you'll go to the sushi takeaway counter.

53
00:02:54,490 --> 00:02:57,110
Charlotte: Will I be preparing boxes of food?

54
00:02:57,110 --> 00:03:00,040
Kaeden: For today, you'll just be helping the staff.

55
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:01,580
Charlotte: Yes, of course.

56
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:05,590
Kaeden: You'll see lots of flat cardboard boxes at one end of the counter.

57
00:03:05,590 --> 00:03:08,730
Kaeden: Beneath those is where we keep the plastic boxes -

58
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:13,440
we run out of those really quickly, so you should bring more from the storeroom.

59
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:16,720
Charlotte: Is that my only task on the sushi counter?

60
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:20,712
Kaeden: No. You also need to clean the area where they prepare the dishes.

61
00:03:20,712 --> 00:03:22,940
There are cloths and bottles of spray by the sink

62
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:26,130
Oh, and please make sure you clean that too.

63
00:03:26,130 --> 00:03:28,820
Charlotte: Sure. That's important, isn't it?

64
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:31,489
Kaeden: Absolutely. But you mustn't wash up knives.

65
00:03:31,489 --> 00:03:35,640
You have to do some training before you're allowed to touch sharp objects.

66
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:38,190
Charlotte: What should I do if there are any?

67
00:03:38,190 --> 00:03:40,210
Kaeden: Ask someone to put them in the dishwasher.

68
00:03:40,210 --> 00:03:43,670
Charlotte: OK, thanks. I don't want to get anything wrong.

69
00:03:43,670 --> 00:03:46,720
Kaeden: Don't worry. You'll be fine. And I'll be around to help.

70
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:47,750
Charlotte: Right.

71
00:03:47,750 --> 00:03:50,432
Kaeden: Finally, the meat and fish counters.

72
00:03:50,432 --> 00:03:53,880
You need to clean the area where staff serve customers

73
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:56,180
including wiping the weighing scales.

74
00:03:56,180 --> 00:03:59,280
Charlotte: OK. Anything else?

75
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:01,580
Kaeden: The fish is laid on ice

76
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:05,860
but when that starts to melt, you'll need to get more from the cold-room.

77
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:09,160
Charlotte: I know the staff on the food counters wear a hat

78
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:11,670
Will that be the same for me?

79
00:04:11,670 --> 00:04:14,630
Kaeden: You won't be serving customers directly, so no.

80
00:04:14,630 --> 00:04:16,720
Kaeden: But make sure you put on thermal gloves

81
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:19,271
when you take anything out of the cold-room.

82
00:04:19,271 --> 00:04:22,820
The temperature's low enough in there to get frostbite from touching things.

83
00:04:22,820 --> 00:04:24,950
Charlotte: Understoood.
